WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.238 --> 00:00:03.060
(tranquil music)

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.000
- [Narrator] Located in Sicily, Italy,

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.749
is an ancient cemetery.

00:00:06.749 --> 00:00:09.960
But to see it, don't look to the ground;

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.141
look up into the valley walls.

00:00:12.141 --> 00:00:14.891
(tranquil music)

00:00:19.312 --> 00:00:23.070
Necropolis di Pantalica is
made up of around 5,000 tombs

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.660
that are carved into
a limestone rock face,

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:27.610
some of which are
believed to have been made

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.651
more than 3,000 years ago.

00:00:29.651 --> 00:00:31.980
(tranquil music)

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.620
The tombs are built like artificial caves,

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.840
small in size and are either square,

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.451
rectangular, or elliptical in shape.

00:00:39.451 --> 00:00:41.010
(tranquil music)

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:44.920
The surrounding area is lush
with native flora and wildlife

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.669
and is completely unspoiled
by infrastructure.

00:00:47.669 --> 00:00:48.990
(tranquil music)

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:52.943
It was listed as a UNESCO
World Heritage Site in 2005.

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:57.440
Currently, the site is
accessible by foot only.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.450
However, a walk through this valley

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.547
is a reflective trip back in time.

00:01:02.547 --> 00:01:05.297
(tranquil music)

